  "behavior": [
    "Core creates the original TextStepContext before preparation and invokes bind_text_preparation_run after admission inside the same Admission readiness result, before prompt/sampler creation or mutable exposure.",
    "MLX binds retained InferenceTextPreparation through the cold hook. No-request unbudgeted preparation remains a no-op and native allocation entry remains unquoted.",
    "The existing TextPreparationAuthority now has one Mutex covering prompt/sampler stages, original run binding and monotone prediction progress. Cold binding cannot race stage construction; late, duplicate and noninitial binding reject.",
    "InferenceTextStep requires original run/policy, ready stages, no active/fenced attempt, exact ordinal, phase and output allowance. Successful issuance consumes ordinal/quota before callbacks or agreement; unfinished Drop permanently fences without refund.",
    "Decode requires the exact preceding completed InferenceTextStepReceipt. Receipts can describe provisional outputs but cannot authorize a successor before finish. Their identity and ordinal retain no request charge or native payload; the live step separately retains its request.",
    "Neutral behavioral tests use genuine core-issued contexts and actual ordinary/controlled drivers, including pre-first-step mutation, callback error/unwind, old/foreign/forked/restored context rejection, stale/provisional/foreign receipts, quota, clone lifetimes and eight-thread single-winner claims.",
    "Existing bounded prefill and preparation tests verify preserved chunk/state/cancellation behavior and concurrent stage/start ownership after replacing atomic stage fields with the shared mutex."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Public strict native managed-memory admission still returns UnknownBound. This increment does not enable a complete native quoted run or change the four ignored positive strict-budget cases.",
    "The runtime grant enforces logical ordering and quota only. MLX does not yet consume these claims in native step permits or attach predecessor receipts to native tokens.",
    "A complete native quote must bind the actual controller/filter, sampling, instrumentation/publication policy, parameter version, domains and input/state frontier. Retained reservations or receipt identity alone cannot select quoted allocation.",
    "Legacy PrefillDriver entry retains its request-level behavior; full quoted native ingress must separately require the current run claim. Raw native/session entry continues to acquire unquoted authority.",
    "Native receipt publication/copy preservation, quoted submission resources, complete preparation/instrumentation bounds, nonempty-state handoff, independent copies and media/paging/distributed/escaped-output accounting remain unfinished.",
    "No new released-checkpoint comparison, peak-memory benchmark or native distributed execution was performed. One portable tokenizer fixture also remains ignored because it requires its external checkpoint."
  ],
